# Flujo de ejemplo de la API. Se corre con REST Client (VS Code) o el HTTP client de IntelliJ.
# Los tokens se guardan solos entre requests. Ajustá las fechas si ya pasaron (validamos @Future).

# En Docker la app queda en 18080; si la corrés nativa (perfil dev) es 8080.
@host = http://localhost:18080

### 1. Registro de un USER
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ana@test.sv", "password": "secret1", "fullName": "Ana Prueba" }

### 2. Login del ADMIN sembrado por Flyway -> guarda el token
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@coworking.sv", "password": "admin1234" }

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 3. Login del USER -> guarda su token
# @name loginUser
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ana@test.sv", "password": "secret1" }

> {% client.global.set("userToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 4. El ADMIN crea un espacio (un USER acá recibiria 403)
POST {{host}}/spaces
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sala Santa Ana", "type": "MEETING_ROOM", "capacity": 10, "location": "Piso 4", "hourlyRate": 15.00 }

### 5. El USER lista los espacios
GET {{host}}/spaces
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 6. El USER crea una reserva (espacio 1 = Sala Izalco, sembrado)
# @name crearReserva
POST {{host}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "spaceId": 1, "startTime": "2027-05-10T09:00:00Z", "endTime": "2027-05-10T11:00:00Z" }

> {% client.global.set("reservaId", response.body.id); %}

### 7. Intento de solape en el mismo espacio y horario -> se espera 409
POST {{host}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "spaceId": 1, "startTime": "2027-05-10T10:00:00Z", "endTime": "2027-05-10T12:00:00Z" }

### 8. Confirmar la reserva -> valida el pago (circuit breaker) y dispara la notificacion async
POST {{host}}/reservations/{{reservaId}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 9. El USER ve sus reservas
GET {{host}}/reservations/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 10. Un id ajeno / inexistente -> se espera 404 (no 403, para no filtrar existencia)
GET {{host}}/reservations/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 11. El ADMIN lista todas, filtrando por estado
GET {{host}}/reservations?status=CONFIRMED
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 12. Reporte de ocupacion (cacheado). Corrélo dos veces para ver la cache.
GET {{host}}/reports/occupancy?from=2027-05-01&to=2027-05-31
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 13. Cancelar la reserva
POST {{host}}/reservations/{{reservaId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 14. Estado del circuit breaker (solo ADMIN)
GET {{host}}/actuator/circuitbreakers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
